{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Sunshine go away today
I don’t feel much like [D]dancing
[G]Some man’s gone, he’s tried to run my life
Don’t know what he’s [C]asking
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]He tells me I’d better get in line
Can’t hear what he’s [D]saying
When [G]I grow up I’m going to make it mine
But these aren’t dues I been [C]paying
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]How much does it cost,[G] I’ll buy it
The [C]time is all we’ve lost,[G] I’ll try it
But [C]he can’t even run[G] his own life
I’ll be [F]damned if he’ll run mine,[D] Sunshine
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Sunshine go away today
I don’t feel much like [D]dancing
[G]Some man’s gone, he’s tried to run my life
Don’t know what he’s [C]asking
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Working starts to make me wonder where
The fruits of what I do are [D]going
[G]He says in love and war all is fair
But he’s got cards he ain’t [C]showing
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]How much does it cost,[G] I’ll buy it
The [C]time is all we’ve lost,[G] I’ll try it
But [C]he can’t even run[G] his own life
I’ll be [F]damned if he’ll run mine,[D] Sunshine
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Sunshine come on back another day
I promise you I’ll be [D]singing
[G]This old world, she’s gonna turn around
Brand new bells’ll be [C]ringing
{end_of_verse}


